          "field": "usage_note",
          "verdict": "issue",
          "quote": "**Wildlife** is a noun for wild animals, and sometimes plants, in general; do not use it as an adjective.",
          "severity": "minor",
          "family": "usage-note",
          "reason": "'Wildlife' is very commonly used as a noun adjunct before another noun ('a wildlife park', 'wildlife conservation'), so telling learners 'do not use it as an adjective' is misleading; it also duplicates the learner_errors note."
